{
 "what": "ANIMATION [everybody idles] (rule 130(a), Paolo 10/23: 'we need a lot of idle animations; right now everyone's standing still, making my brain fry; it's looking like a chess man and I don't want that vibe at all'). THE KEPT SOURCE OF EVERY IDLE (rule 128): each pose is bone turns on the rig's man (the skeleton every person in the game is built on), each clip is held keys, three a beat at 120. tools/bohemia_animation_everybody_idles.py lays them on any man and DIRECTION's master rig renders them; an era is a re-render, never a redraw.",
 "axes": "the poses tool's axes (tools/bohemia_combat_the_fight_poses.py): F forward, U up, L the man's left, in the armature's space. [bone, axis, deg] turns a bone (and what hangs off it) about the axis through its own head, root first; about L +deg leans the chest forward and -deg brings a hanging arm up in front; about U +deg turns toward his left; about F +deg lifts his left side (the left arm out, the left hip up), -deg the right arm out. ['MOVE', bone, [f, u, l]] slides a bone in metres. After every pose the feet are put back where they stood (two-bone IK, knees forward), so nobody skates.",
